\item[(b)] $\ensuremath{\mathop{\pmb{K}}}$ has few maximal models, 

\item[(c)] if ${\ensuremath{\mathcal{M}}} \in K_{-\infty}$ then ${\ensuremath{\mathcal{M}}}$ is eventually determined with respect to $\ensuremath{\mathop{\pmb{K}}}$, and

\item[(d)] for every invariant $Q \in \ensuremath{\mathfrak{L}}_b$ there is some ${\ensuremath{\mathcal{M}}} \in K$ where ${\ensuremath{\mathcal{M}}} \models (\exists {\bm{x}})\, Q({\bm{x}})$. 
\end{itemize}

