A {\bf{plan}} on a non-empty set $A$ is a finitary convex geometry ${\ensuremath{\mathcal{P}}} \subseteq \raisebox{.15\baselineskip}{\Large\ensuremath{\wp}}_{<\ensuremath{\omega}}(A)$ in which every closed set of size at least $2$ has precisely two extreme points. In other words: $\emptyset \in {\ensuremath{\mathcal{P}}}$, we have $\bigcup {\ensuremath{\mathcal{P}}} = A$,  the geometry ${\ensuremath{\mathcal{P}}}$ is closed under intersections, every finite set is contained in some closed set, and its closure operator $\operatorname{cl}_{{\ensuremath{\mathcal{P}}}}$ satisfies 
\begin{itemize}
\item (Convexity) $(\forall B \in {\ensuremath{\mathcal{P}}})(\forall x, y \in A \setminus B)\, (x \neq y) \ensuremath{\wedge} \bigl(x \in \operatorname{cl}_{{\ensuremath{\mathcal{P}}}}(B \cup \{y\})\bigr) \rightarrow \bigl(y \not \in \operatorname{cl}_{{\ensuremath{\mathcal{P}}}}(B \cup \{x\})\bigr)$, and

\item (Extreme Points) $(\forall B \in {\ensuremath{\mathcal{P}}}, |B| \geq 2)\, |\{ b \in B \,:\, B \setminus \{b\} \in {\ensuremath{\mathcal{P}}}\}| = 2$. 
\end{itemize}

